The coronavirus pandemic exacerbated the social inequalities related to insufficient connectivity: privileged users experienced dropped calls and disrupted downloads, while disadvantaged users were left with no access at all or with makeshift solutions.</p><p style="text-align:right"><br/><span style=""><em>Internet: &lt;www.europarl.europa.eu/thinktank&gt; (adapted).</em></span></p></div><p style="text-align: left;">Based on the <strong>text CB1A2-II,</strong> judge the following item.</p><p style="text-align: left;">Digital divide can be understood as the lack of long-term stable connection to the Internet.</p>', 'judge the following item. Digital divide can be understood as the lack of long-term stable connection to the Internet.', true, '2026-01-30 18:26:23.6685', '2026-01-30 18:26:23.6685', 'ERRADO', '', false);
