Phaidon, New York – London: 1995, p. 7-8 (adapted).</span></p></div><p>Considering text II, judge whether the following statement are right (C) or wrong (E).</p><p style="text-align: left;">By stating that he wants to show the reader “the lie of the land” (first sentence of the text), the author means that he wants to inform the reader of the rules he followed in writing the book.</p>', 'judge whether the', true, '2026-01-30 18:26:23.6685', '2026-01-30 18:26:23.6685', 'ERRADO', '', false);
INSERT INTO public.questao VALUES (29796, 1994, 3797, '3082454', NULL, 'CEBRASPE', '<div style="display: block; border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 10px; margin: 10px 0;"><p><strong>Text II</strong></p><p style="text-align: left;"><br/>
